  "prefLabel": "Inst 103.06 Duties of the Board",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Inst 103.06 Duties of the Board.\n\n(a) The statutory responsibilities of the board created by RSA 205-D:2, V and RSA 205-D:3 shall include but are not limited to:\n\n(1) Adopting rules and regulations to administer RSA 205-D in accordance with RSA 541-A;\n\n(2) Establishing licensing qualifications and standards for manufactured housing installers;\n\n(3) Setting standards for installation including but not limited to, supports, anchoring, and underpinning of manufactured houses installed in this state;\n\n(4) Establishing requirements for inspections;\n\n(5) Undertaking disciplinary proceedings in accordance with Plc 200;\n\n(6) Establishing requirements on forms as necessary; and\n\n(7) Developing and providing a program to train and educate installers or referring to a board approved program developed and taught by a private agency.\n\n(8) Developing and providing alternative dispute resolution.\n\nSource. #8492, eff 12-24-05; amd by #10336, eff 5-15-13; ss by #14111, eff 1-17-25",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/inst100-700.html"
